cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PIM-AutoDSE in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: "PIM-AutoDSE: Automated ISA and Design Space Exploration for PIM"
abstract: >-
  Processing-in-memory (PIM) offers a promising solution to the memory wall,
  but the Instruction Set Architecture (ISA) of PIM has never been
  systematically evaluated. PIM ISA choices - such as instruction fusion -
  directly affect DRAM read/write operations: an unfused instruction spills its
  intermediate result back to the DRAM array, and each spill costs an
  ACTIVATE/PRECHARGE pair that inflates application runtime and energy. We
  present PIM-AutoDSE, a retargetable framework that extends PIMeval, a PIM
  simulator, to provide cycle-accurate performance and energy analysis
  supporting features including instruction fusion, register contention, and
  prefetching. PIM-AutoDSE further extends the synthesis-based compiler MISAAL
  to provide code generation from high-level languages to diverse PIM
  architectures, and proposes a methodology for PIM ISA synthesis from
  pseudocode to automatically generate RISC- and CISC-like ISAs. Using
  PIM-AutoDSE, we conduct the first systematic study of instruction fusion for
  PIM, demonstrating up to 2.7x improvement in execution runtime and energy
  over non-fused baselines across different workloads.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/UVA-LavaLab/PIM-AutoDSE"

